    "q8-once"
  ],
  "text": "Question eight. When do you introduce a message queue? When work doesn't need to finish inside the request. Counting clicks in the database makes every redirect wait on a write, and sends a viral link's whole spike there. Queue each click instead. The redirect returns at once, workers drain the queue at their own pace, and a burst just makes it longer. Slow work, like email or video transcoding, goes the same way. The price is at-least-once delivery: a worker that crashes before acknowledging gets the click again. So make the consumer idempotent: give each click an ID, and record the ID in the same transaction that adds to the count, so a repeat changes nothing. The totals now run a little behind.",
